00:00:48.660 --> 00:00:54.540
with work beginning in September. Immediate action is to review project files for any

00:00:54.540 --> 00:01:00.400
current or planned marine terminal assessments in British Columbia. Consultants handling federal

00:01:00.400 --> 00:01:06.100
port projects, marine sediment assessments, and oil transport infrastructure in British Columbia

00:01:06.100 --> 00:01:11.900
are most affected. Vancouver Port Authority granted permission to dredge beneath the second

00:01:11.900 --> 00:01:18.520
narrows bridge in barrage inlet. Dredging will enable larger oil tankers to increase loads through the

00:01:18.520 --> 00:01:24.480
